WEBVTT

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:08.110
There's a mysterious cosplay group 
causing a ruckus around the school lately...

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:12.580
Their identities aren't visible 
to the naked eye or in pictures.

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:16.980
This could be interesting material.

00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:52.930
To Steal Love Without Regret

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.090
Raining again today?

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:13.830
It is the rainy season, after all.

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:16.430
It's hard to be enthusiastic when it's raining.

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:17.330
About what?

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:19.870
Active and aggressive things.

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:22.630
In all the time I've known you,

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:26.110
I've never seen you do anything 
active and aggressive.

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:27.170
Really?

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:31.580
The Yufuin En I know is 
always passive and defensive.

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:34.680
That's my Atsushi. 
He's got the English skills.

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:37.590
Apparently, "naïve" and "sensitive"

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.340
are not considered compliments
in the English-speaking world.

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:42.810
People say stuff like
"a naïve young man," though.

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:46.730
Over there, that means "a careless young man."

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:47.730
Exactly!

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:49.690
Why are you looking at me?

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:51.680
It just seemed appropriate.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:55.540
Io, I am not a careless young man.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:57.840
I am a guileless young man.

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:00.200
You have a wonderfully high opinion of yourself.

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:02.610
Totally losing my motivation...

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:04.840
I'm telling you, you never had any.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:11.990
Yumoto?

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:15.840
Were your pupils dilated just now?

00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:21.360
Something about touching Wom-san 
takes me closer to Nirvana.

00:03:22.030 --> 00:03:24.240
Like Linus's blanket?

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:26.180
Oh, yeah, like a feeling of security?

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:29.490
It's a little different from security.

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:30.720
Then what is it?

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:32.080
What, indeed?

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:33.720
You're asking me?

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:36.860
I say "no thank you" to being cuddled for no reason!

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:39.150
Don't say that!

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.150
Unhand me, you!

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:41.070
Let me cuddle you!

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:44.080
Day after day after day, 
you've cuddled me so much,

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:47.080
the fur around my stomach is thinning out!

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:49.090
Then I'll do your back from now on!

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:52.020
That is not the issue!

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:53.970
Does it absolutely have to be Wombat?

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:55.760
Could it be something else?

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:58.320
Hmm! Good question!

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:02.420
Something about his cuddliness 
is just right to me.

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:04.260
Gives me that "feel so fine" feeling!

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:06.510
What if he were some other kind of fluffy?

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:08.420
I'd consider it.

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:09.700
Floofy?

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:11.490
Absolutely!

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:12.640
Fuzzy?

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:13.940
That would be fine.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:15.840
Like that over there?

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:17.940
Oh, that's good!

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:19.940
Wait, that's...

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:23.360
Mr. Tawarayama!

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:24.560
What is all this?

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:26.770
Mold? Is it mold? It's mold!

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:28.030
Hey, hey, hey!

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:29.580
Cut it out!

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:32.950
Wombat, what happened
to your advanced science?

00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:34.930
I'm sorry!

00:04:34.930 --> 00:04:37.170
The high temperature and humidity lately

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:39.970
have created favorable 
conditions for mold growth!

00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:42.920
"Favorable"? It's utterly putrid.

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:47.310
It's fine! Get rid of the mold and 
the main body will still be fine!

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:50.130
The hyphae of mold go down 
deeper than you'd think.

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:53.350
One time, I picked the mold off some 
bread and ate it, and I got sick!

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:54.840
Are you stupid?

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:56.370
I was hungry!

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:59.060
Anyway, it's bad that he's growing mold, isn't it?

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:00.860
Let's wash him! Let's wash him!

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:02.910
Everything turns out okay after a washing!

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:07.320
What's this? What color is this?

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:11.280
Wombat, you have to be more 
careful with Mr. Tawarayama.

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:12.720
Yeah, there's no love in this.

00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:17.730
You say that I, who came here to fill 
the Earth with love, have no love?!

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:18.560
Nope, none.

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:19.710
Crude in every way.

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:20.720
Upsy-daisy!

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:24.640
Hey. He fell.

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:27.410
There, it turned out okay!

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:28.560
It did not!

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:31.360
If anyone saw this,
they'd say it was elder abuse!

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:32.560
Assault, right?

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:35.980
<b>Earth Defense Club         (lol)</b>

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:35.600
He just looks that way because 
he's wet. If we dry him off...

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:40.040
I thought I just heard a knock.

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:43.640
But no one's ever visited us before.

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:46.960
Either way, this situation clearly looks bad!

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:49.120
All Hell's gonna break loose, yeah.

00:05:50.210 --> 00:05:51.990
Pardon me!

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:55.270
Man, he sure is persistent!

00:05:55.270 --> 00:05:56.090
Hey!

00:05:58.130 --> 00:06:00.460
Who's there? What do you want?

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:02.530
Oh, how rude of me.

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:05.840
I am Kinosaki of the PS.

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:07.190
PS?

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:09.010
The Press Society.

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:11.320
This is my photographer, Tazawa.

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:12.110
Hey.

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:13.770
<b>Binan High School
Press Society 
Kinosaki Kou</b>

00:06:12.110 --> 00:06:13.770
A pleasure to make your acquaintance.

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:17.230
And what do two members of
the Press Society want with us?

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:18.750
How rude of me.

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:22.850
The truth is, I publish online articles
for the Binan High School Press Society

00:06:22.850 --> 00:06:26.450
about daily life on campus.

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:28.350
Online?

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:31.320
The other day at a meeting, 
I proposed a new project:

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:34.360
could we make a theme out of the 
"bonds" between distinctive teachers

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:36.790
and the students around them?

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:40.590
I call it "Beloved Teachers"!

00:06:40.590 --> 00:06:43.470
Well? Don't you think it's a great project?

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:44.760
Yeah...

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:46.920
Thank you for the words of praise.

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:51.970
A flower of compassion blooming 
quietly in the wild concrete jungle...

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:55.220
The bond between student and
teacher is the most precious of all!

00:06:55.220 --> 00:06:57.080
"My teacher!" "My class!"

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:59.240
Souls crying out to each other!

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:00.440
A miraculous meeting!

00:07:00.740 --> 00:07:02.440
This guy's weird.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:03.900
You're one to talk.

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:05.580
Don't let it worry you.

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:08.710
The press is often misunderstood.

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:14.310
But to root out the truth and 
convey it in elaborate, minute detail...

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:17.620
I believe that is our mission.

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:20.470
Hey, what are you doing?

00:07:20.470 --> 00:07:22.620
I refuse to have my picture taken.

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:26.540
No, I just received your consent to be covered.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:28.210
I thought we'd get started right away.

00:07:28.450 --> 00:07:29.370
Covered?

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:30.350
Consent?

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:31.090
Who gave it?

00:07:31.090 --> 00:07:32.710
Oh, honestly!

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:35.730
Right now, you just said it
was a good project, didn't you?

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:39.650
Now, let's get right to the 
interview wth Mr. Tawarayama!

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:45.110
Mr. Tawarayama, from all that I've just seen,

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:49.280
you seem to enjoy a very frank 
relationship with your students.

00:07:49.670 --> 00:07:50.940
What you've just seen?

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:51.810
Yes.

00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:55.680
I was below when I caught sight of 
the fun you were having by the window.

00:07:57.020 --> 00:08:02.370
Mr. Tawarayama, you seem truly 
energetic for a man of your age.

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:07.220
Please, tell us the secret of 
your health and agile movements.

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:10.400
Mr. Tawarayama?

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:13.090
We decline this interview.

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:15.740
We're a boring club. 
No one's going to find it interesting.

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:16.850
No, no.

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:20.770
It is the users who will determine 
what's interesting and what's not.

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:22.150
Please leave.

00:08:22.150 --> 00:08:23.520
If you don't...

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:26.810
Um, you can refuse if you want to, but...

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:29.940
I have a little something 
called freedom of the press.

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:33.120
So I'm going to gather material 
without hesitation. Okay?

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:38.080
It's a violation of our likeness usage rights.

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:40.020
Nowadays, you have to be very careful

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:42.160
about how you use personal information.

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:48.390
Yes. That's why I thought it would be 
beneficial for you to use us, as well.

00:08:48.390 --> 00:08:50.300
Let's make it a win-win situation!

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:56.340
<i>Oh, dear...</i>

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.530
Good morning, Yufuin-san!

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:06.180
It seems we're finally getting a bit of 
a break from the rainy season, eh?

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:08.240
Are you feeling well, Yufuin-san?

00:09:09.450 --> 00:09:12.740
Come to think of it, 
I don't see Kinugawa-san around.

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:14.240
Are you all alone, Yufuin-san?

00:09:14.670 --> 00:09:15.990
Atsushi has day duty.

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:17.200
So what do you want?

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:19.040
How rude of me.

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:21.710
I'm here for your morning 
greeting and interview.

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:23.150
Interview?

00:09:23.150 --> 00:09:27.390
Yes. Yufuin En-san, what are your hobbies?

00:09:27.390 --> 00:09:29.780
Hobbies? None, really.

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:31.140
Special skills?

00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:32.850
Special skills? None, really.

00:09:32.850 --> 00:09:35.060
He says he has no real skills.

00:09:35.060 --> 00:09:37.860
Uh, I don't like you putting it that way...

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:39.370
Favorite foods?

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:40.550
Well, none really.

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:41.870
He has no favorite foods.

00:09:41.870 --> 00:09:42.930
Look, I told you...

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:45.930
You're not giving me much of an interview.

00:09:45.930 --> 00:09:48.380
Well, you can't just ask me 
this stuff out of the blue.

00:09:48.860 --> 00:09:51.260
Give me some questions 
that are easier to answer.

00:09:51.260 --> 00:09:53.430
Questions that are easier to answer?

00:09:53.430 --> 00:09:55.330
Let me see...

00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:58.640
If you suddenly became a superhero 
tasked with protecting the Earth,

00:09:58.640 --> 00:09:59.610
what would you do?

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:03.750
Well, it's a purely hypothetical question.

00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:07.250
What would you do if something 
like that were to happen?

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:12.600
Are you the type that would find 
it bothersome? Or would you...

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:17.470
That pose... Discomfort? Despair?!

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:21.930
It's the rage, fury, and indignation 
over a failed FX transaction!

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:23.670
You're so stupid.

00:10:23.670 --> 00:10:26.200
Don't cry. I hate women who cry.

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:30.060
Even if he became a superhero, 
he'd hate women who cry, he says.

00:10:30.580 --> 00:10:32.960
I can buy you a remote control, at least.

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:35.910
Huh? Are remote controls that expensive?

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:37.700
Then just do it by hand.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:41.450
It's tough when you can't 
change from hot air to cold.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:44.730
Why can't you just put it 
on an automatic setting?

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:48.090
Carefully adjusting your settings is better 
for the environment, don't you think?

00:10:48.590 --> 00:10:50.080
Shut up!

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:52.210
Hello? Hello?

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:55.570
Your defense of romance failed, I see.

00:10:55.570 --> 00:10:56.880
Save it!

00:10:57.480 --> 00:10:58.800
What is that?

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:01.380
Like part of a "ten questions" thing?

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:04.940
No, no. Nothing so sophisticated.

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:08.000
Good point. That would 
make a boring question.

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:10.770
Oh, you got one on me there.

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:17.950
I can't eat any more...

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:22.410
Huh?

00:11:22.690 --> 00:11:25.390
Just ten more minutes...

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:27.330
What, what?

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:39.250
I am a puppet under my father's control.

00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:41.530
<b>Sousa Enkaku</b>

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:41.810
I can only follow the rails he's laid for me.

00:11:41.810 --> 00:11:43.320
Is that so?

00:11:47.210 --> 00:11:50.710
Then perhaps it's time you did the controlling.

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:56.900
<b>Io Naruko
Born December 17th
Blood Type A / Capricorn
Hobbies: Financial investment and management
Likes: Money, beef bowls</b>

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:05.040
They're... Or, I should say <i>he</i>'s annoying.

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:09.140
He's awful. In the last two days, 
I've suffered a loss of 1.8 million.

00:12:09.140 --> 00:12:12.250
I wish he'd disappear. Just turn to dust.

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:13.580
Really!

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:18.030
With those two hanging around, 
I can't act freely at all!

00:12:18.030 --> 00:12:22.640
I have to stay close to that 
individual, and I can't even talk!

00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:25.300
I'm so restricted! I feel so trapped!

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:29.730
You may as well call it oppression!
We must do something at once!

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:31.900
Isn't this reaping what you sow?

00:12:32.470 --> 00:12:35.440
It's okay. I'll cuddle you in exchange.

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:36.800
That ain't the point!

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:39.920
They didn't come see me for an interview.

00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:41.130
I would've answered, too.

00:12:41.130 --> 00:12:43.410
You were just sleepin' like a baby!

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:46.930
I've never seen Wombat so pissed off.

00:12:46.930 --> 00:12:49.800
When he gets pissed off, 
he talks with a Kansai accent, then?

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:53.330
It's fine to rant, but please don't 
leave Mr. Tawarayama like that.

00:12:53.670 --> 00:12:56.460
Really, you keep cooling 
him off and heating him up...

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:57.760
What are you sayin'?

00:12:57.760 --> 00:13:01.460
An hour or two away from him ain't 
gonna make a difference at this point!

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:03.160
Wombat's gone delinquent!

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:05.050
Hey, what's wrong with you—

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:06.730
Don't touch me!

00:13:06.730 --> 00:13:08.990
Jackass! Your mama's got an outie!

00:13:08.990 --> 00:13:12.600
The stress is causing Wombat 
to resort to name calling!

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:14.530
He's being pretty careless.

00:13:14.530 --> 00:13:16.880
Does that make him naïve?

00:13:18.710 --> 00:13:19.860
Hello!

00:13:21.640 --> 00:13:24.700
Is this what they call a "naked hang-out"?

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:27.860
The Kurotama Bath. 
It's a fine location, isn't it?

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:30.620
We're going to take 
advantage of it in a big way!

00:13:31.590 --> 00:13:35.250
So the Defense Club is taking a 
bath along with their pink pet.

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:37.550
How nice! Talk about a fine picture!

00:13:37.910 --> 00:13:41.160
And Mr. Tawarayama has a very 
distinctive bathing style.

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:48.940
Excuse me, Kinosaki-san.

00:13:48.940 --> 00:13:53.190
This is a private gathering. 
Could you please refrain from doing this?

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:54.800
Oh, how rude of me.

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:57.990
Of course, whether you participate 
or not is your own choice.

00:13:58.220 --> 00:14:01.430
Well, outsiders are not really... you know?

00:14:01.430 --> 00:14:04.260
Oh? Does this place have a membership system?

00:14:04.260 --> 00:14:06.950
No, it's not that...

00:14:07.390 --> 00:14:11.670
But Mr. Tawarayama sure can hold 
his breath a long time, can't he?

00:14:15.010 --> 00:14:17.630
Seriously? At a time like this?

00:14:17.630 --> 00:14:19.520
This is the usual Lovra—

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:22.430
Love? What was that? What was that?

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:24.460
Um, well...

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:27.170
Mr. Tawarayama's spent 
too long in the hot water.

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:28.820
Why don't we cool him down a while?

00:14:28.820 --> 00:14:30.810
Yes, yes, let's do that.

00:14:30.810 --> 00:14:32.100
Ah, but...

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:33.780
C'mon, Mr. Tawarayama!

00:14:33.780 --> 00:14:35.780
You don't want to get dizzy.

00:14:33.780 --> 00:14:36.520
Let's take a break over there.

00:14:37.280 --> 00:14:39.170
We'll be back soon.

00:14:39.170 --> 00:14:42.450
Please, enjoy the bath, you two.

00:14:42.450 --> 00:14:46.280
Hurry! Love Making into the Battle Lovers!

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:48.370
Calm down, Wombat.

00:14:48.370 --> 00:14:50.660
There's no way we can transform here.

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:54.710
But while we're standing here,
love is, love was, love will be...

00:14:55.050 --> 00:14:57.520
If we transform now, they'll find us out.

00:14:57.520 --> 00:14:59.790
I bet he's already suspicious of us.

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:01.280
Would it be bad if they found out?

00:15:01.280 --> 00:15:02.460
Of course.

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:03.680
If they find out...

00:15:03.680 --> 00:15:05.880
What's with those outfits?

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:08.250
Is there a point to the big speeches?

00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:09.600
How does it feel?

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:11.600
You guys!

00:15:11.880 --> 00:15:13.240
No way.

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:17.680
That hurts, darn it!

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:19.270
Can't we turn these things off?

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:22.240
It won't stop until you end 
it with the Love Shower!

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:23.890
This sucks.

00:15:23.890 --> 00:15:25.940
If we don't hurry, they'll finish their bath!

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:27.820
We'll just have to kill him.

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:28.950
Huh?

00:15:28.950 --> 00:15:29.880
Who?

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:33.510
Mr. Tawarayama. He'll have to die for us!

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:35.170
Oh...

00:15:35.590 --> 00:15:37.160
No way!

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:38.790
How frightening!

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:40.830
Isn't that a little out of date?

00:15:41.310 --> 00:15:43.840
Now, now. Just hear me out.

00:15:44.650 --> 00:15:46.670
What are they talking about?

00:15:48.740 --> 00:15:49.760
What happened?

00:15:50.060 --> 00:15:51.810
Mr. Tawarayama...

00:15:51.810 --> 00:15:54.480
Mr. Tawarayama isn't breathing!

00:15:56.910 --> 00:15:58.970
Look, Kinosaki-san!

00:15:58.970 --> 00:16:03.150
See? He's not breathing, right?
And his pupils are dilated!

00:16:03.510 --> 00:16:05.720
Go on! Check and make sure!

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:10.110
Do it! It's the press's job to get to the truth!

00:16:10.450 --> 00:16:12.360
Th-That is true...

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:14.840
Y-You're right. It's not beating.

00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:17.090
This is awful!

00:16:17.720 --> 00:16:20.970
So, we're going to go call a doctor!

00:16:20.970 --> 00:16:23.540
Please stay with Mr. Tawarayama until then!

00:16:24.930 --> 00:16:26.450
Let's go, Defense Club!

00:16:26.450 --> 00:16:29.900
Let's defend Mr. Tawarayama's life and health!

00:16:29.900 --> 00:16:30.800
Yeah!

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:32.310
Hey, wai—

00:16:34.370 --> 00:16:35.400
Hey! Go after them!

00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:37.400
But we're naked.

00:16:37.400 --> 00:16:39.400
They're naked, too!

00:16:43.920 --> 00:16:44.750
Now!

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:46.500
Love Making!

00:16:49.390 --> 00:16:51.360
You, who befoul our beloved Earth!

00:16:51.850 --> 00:16:53.580
No justice can come from loveless power!

00:16:54.100 --> 00:16:55.330
Love is all!

00:16:55.890 --> 00:16:57.740
Live for love! Die for love!

00:16:58.130 --> 00:17:00.870
We are the heirs to the throne of love!

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:02.330
Battle Lovers!

00:17:02.860 --> 00:17:04.180
Feel the power...

00:17:04.840 --> 00:17:06.480
Of love!

00:17:08.320 --> 00:17:09.250
Oh, come on!

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:11.920
We don't need to do the introduction 
if we're transforming in secret!

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:13.420
Besides, we don't have time!

00:17:13.420 --> 00:17:15.770
It's a matter of feeling and etiquette!

00:17:15.770 --> 00:17:17.390
Let's go!

00:17:21.860 --> 00:17:23.080
There!

00:17:29.220 --> 00:17:30.140
It's hot.

00:17:30.140 --> 00:17:31.810
What is this?

00:17:33.460 --> 00:17:35.530
The air conditioner! And it's hot air!

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:37.780
Who hit the heater button?

00:17:40.320 --> 00:17:42.390
Touching the control panel directly...

00:17:42.390 --> 00:17:48.250
You hate that minor task so much, 
you invented the remote control to avoid it.

00:17:48.780 --> 00:17:51.650
But in exchange for that slight saving of time,

00:17:51.650 --> 00:17:54.720
you also invite a great threat...

00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:57.620
Air conditioners that can't cool in the summer!

00:17:57.620 --> 00:17:59.890
Video games that can't get 
past the title screen!

00:17:59.890 --> 00:18:02.840
Bidet toilets that won't 
stop washing your butthole!

00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:05.980
TVs locked forever on TV Tokyo!

00:18:07.410 --> 00:18:10.140
Now, let's make things a little warmer!

00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:13.690
It's hot...

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:14.630
So hot...

00:18:19.890 --> 00:18:21.700
Battle Lover Kick!

00:18:26.190 --> 00:18:28.870
You are really, really, 
really, really long-winded!

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:30.420
We're in a hurry, you know!

00:18:30.980 --> 00:18:34.340
If you don't have a remote control, 
just pull the plug and consider from there!

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:35.050
That was fast.

00:18:35.050 --> 00:18:36.210
One hit?

00:18:36.210 --> 00:18:38.650
It's like there was no 
reason for us to be here.

00:18:38.650 --> 00:18:39.640
Seriously.

00:18:39.920 --> 00:18:42.480
Okay! Let's finish this quick!

00:18:42.480 --> 00:18:43.680
I don't think so!

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:47.110
He stopped!

00:18:50.280 --> 00:18:53.940
Did you forget I'm the 
Remote Control Monster?

00:18:55.060 --> 00:18:56.410
My body's moving on its own!

00:18:57.830 --> 00:19:02.370
You are but a puppet that moves 
as my remote control dictates!

00:19:06.130 --> 00:19:07.000
Gulp!

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:08.970
C'mon, c'mon, c'mon, c'mon!

00:19:13.930 --> 00:19:16.420
C'mon, c'mon, c'mon, c'mon!

00:19:17.140 --> 00:19:18.350
Shut up!

00:19:19.460 --> 00:19:20.310
Now!

00:19:20.660 --> 00:19:23.840
Love Attack!

00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:32.810
Love Shower!

00:19:37.710 --> 00:19:41.990
So I was also a mere puppet under their control?

00:19:42.800 --> 00:19:46.000
From now on, I should follow my own will...

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:51.200
Love is over!

00:19:51.200 --> 00:19:52.870
I'm so done objecting to that.

00:19:53.350 --> 00:19:56.850
Hey, this is Sousa Enkaku from class 3-B.

00:19:56.850 --> 00:20:00.030
So the monsters are being 
controlled by someone?

00:20:00.030 --> 00:20:01.390
Who could it be?

00:20:01.750 --> 00:20:03.360
Hey! We have to get back, quick!

00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:04.100
Oh, no!

00:20:08.150 --> 00:20:09.850
What should we do?

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:11.660
For the time being...

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:20.820
Mr. Tawarayama! Have you come to?

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:22.850
How do you feel?

00:20:22.850 --> 00:20:26.180
Ah, hello, my friends. I feel fine.

00:20:26.180 --> 00:20:27.920
That is a fine thing to hear.

00:20:28.250 --> 00:20:30.890
Why are they talking like 
they're in a period drama?

00:20:30.890 --> 00:20:31.900
Who knows?

00:20:31.900 --> 00:20:35.830
Mr. Tawaramura, this is 
Kinosaki-san and Tazawa-san,

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:37.920
who took care of you while you were out.

00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:41.820
So you are my Florence Nightengales?

00:20:41.820 --> 00:20:43.100
N-No...

00:20:43.460 --> 00:20:45.680
We fooled them completely... I guess?

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:46.550
I dunno.

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:49.320
I know! A picture! Let's take a picture!

00:20:49.320 --> 00:20:52.030
Gora! Come here a minute!

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:53.610
What is it, Yumoto?

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:55.920
<i>The Village of the Eight Tombs</i>!

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:57.790
Take our picture for us!

00:20:58.480 --> 00:20:59.500
Sure.

00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:00.530
Let us borrow that.

00:21:01.140 --> 00:21:02.490
Okay, I'm taking it.

00:21:02.490 --> 00:21:03.570
Go for it!

00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:05.710
One, two... snap!

00:21:05.710 --> 00:21:11.460
<b>Earth Defense Club
Defending the Teacher</b>

00:21:11.750 --> 00:21:13.460
What is this?

00:21:13.960 --> 00:21:16.710
"The heartwarming bonds that 
unite the teachers and students

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:18.720
of Binan High School," apparently.

00:21:18.720 --> 00:21:19.880
What nonsense.

00:21:20.370 --> 00:21:22.340
And why are they dressed like this?

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:24.010
It's the height of vulgarity.

00:21:24.010 --> 00:21:26.880
Although it seems to have 
gotten quite a reaction.

00:21:27.240 --> 00:21:28.520
A reaction?

00:21:28.930 --> 00:21:32.760
Yes, along with words of praise
from the neighborhood.

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:36.690
What shall we do, Kinshiro?

00:21:37.570 --> 00:21:42.200
We'll have to accept their 
club application sooner or later.

00:21:46.850 --> 00:21:48.630
{upside-down}By order of the 
Binan High School
Student Council

00:21:47.100 --> 00:21:48.630
Oh, it's upside down.

00:21:50.340 --> 00:21:52.070
Our direct report

00:21:52.070 --> 00:21:55.670
went pretty well for the first stage, didn't it?

00:22:01.600 --> 00:22:02.690
Right?

00:23:40.720 --> 00:23:44.450
If we get bad grades on our finals, 
the Defense Club will be disbanded?!

00:23:44.450 --> 00:23:48.340
And the student council is 
offering me a position as treasurer?

00:23:48.340 --> 00:23:50.720
Sure thing, if you pay me!

00:23:50.720 --> 00:23:53.080
Next time: Love is Something 
You Wear on Your Back.

00:23:50.990 --> 00:23:54.850
Next Time

00:23:50.990 --> 00:23:54.850
Love is Something You Wear on Your Back

00:23:53.080 --> 00:23:54.250
Love Making!
